# =====================================================================================
# abelian_group_law.rq — RED->GREEN probe for T-ABEL (the COMMUTATIVITY tooth, W2 · SP0).
# The characteristic law of the abelian-group rung, over the unified @rel:* reified-table
# vocabulary (bridges.ttl:249-291: relation:structure = fnd:opStructure,
# relation:category:first/second/result = fnd:opLeft/opRight/opResult).
# =====================================================================================
# The ABELIAN-GROUP commutativity law: for a model's reified Cayley table (cells scoped to the
# model by @rel:structure), the product must COMMUTE — for every ordered pair x,y the product
# x·y must equal the swapped product y·x. This SELECT walks the table twice:
#   ?c1 : x·y = p        ?c2 : y·x = q
# and returns every pair whose two orders DISAGREE (p != q) — the model, the two operands and the
# two disagreeing products. It is the folded stratified re-homing of the ONE law the abelian-group
# rung adds over the group (algebra_spine.ttl composition map :99-103,226; design §1.5 commutativity
# axiom, the abelian:group atom — DISTINCT from the commutative-monoid commutativity atom, no-cram).
# abelian-group = group + commutativity; the underlying inverse / identity / associativity / closure
# laws are inherited from the group theory and are policed by probes/group_law.rq,
# probes/monoid_identity.rq and probes/semigroup_law.rq — this probe is the PRIMARY, characteristic-law
# tooth for THIS rung: it detects non-commutativity directly (a non-commutative group is a group but
# NOT an abelian group).
#
#   GREEN (a genuine abelian group, e.g. fixtures/abelian_group_pos.ttl — Z/3 under +):
#         0 rows — every pair commutes, the tooth is satisfied.
#   RED   (a non-commutative fragment, e.g. fixtures/abelian_group_neg.ttl — one cell corrupted so
#         x·y != y·x for some pair): >= 1 row — commutativity fails and the tooth bites.
#
# Run over the algebra data graph merged with the fixture under test, inference=none. The
# commutativity-specific SHACL NodeShape is authored later by T-SHAPES; until then the negative
# fixture's single corrupted cell is chosen to involve the identity element e (e·b), so that the SAME
# one-cell error ALSO trips the existing ModelShape identity tooth (shapes/algebra.shapes.ttl,
# sh:targetClass rec:model:record) — so the runner's fixture iteration (run-algebra-checks.sh
# step (b)) catches it as a non-conforming negative. This probe is the direct commutativity tooth.

PREFIX rel: <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:>

SELECT ?model ?x ?y ?p ?q WHERE {
  # x·y = p
  ?c1 rel:structure       ?model ;
      rel:category:first  ?x ;
      rel:category:second ?y ;
      rel:category:result ?p .
  # y·x = q  (the swapped order)
  ?c2 rel:structure       ?model ;
      rel:category:first  ?y ;
      rel:category:second ?x ;
      rel:category:result ?q .
  FILTER(?p != ?q)   # x·y != y·x  =>  commutativity violated
}
